  CASE=3 huge equal complex operands divide to 1+0i, flags=0.
  CASE=4 (1+i)/(0+0i): both parts +inf; flags=1 for f32, 3 for f64/f128.
    Those 36 executions collect target bits/flags; no result was pre-authorized
    by returning zero. Flags are captured BEFORE printf.
  Both reference compilers and O0/O2 agree within each format on these probes.
  Pair size/alignment: 8/4, 16/8, 32/16 respectively.
  EvoCC component-store forms currently report E1003; constructor CASE=2 E2001.
  This is the observed first-error boundary, not a claim that admitting the
  syntax would already implement arithmetic, helpers or the public ABI.
